Let the Mac shader translation take AIR 1.x libraries.

The Mac fallback (tools/translate_metallib.py, run by serve_shader_translation.py for a
library the iPad refuses) required an MDSZ tag and AIR 2.0 to 2.8, so it refused all
536 of Brighter Shores' libraries ("missing module metadata"), container version 2 with
AIR 1.8 and no MDSZ: the fallback patch 0003 counts on would have failed too. A module
of such a library now runs to the next module or the end of the code section, as
translation/Metal/LegacyMetal.h finds it on the device, and its HASH still has to
match. AIR 1.x has no iOS revision of its own: each module is compiled for iOS 14 as it
is, and where the compiler refuses, through Apple's upgrade pass to AIR 2.3 first (the
route this script already takes for AIR 2.1). Libraries with MDSZ and AIR 2.x take the
same path as before. Whether Apple's tools accept AIR 1.8 has to be seen on a Mac.
Upstream candidate.

